/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
   DAY 1   THE RECKONING IN THE IRON GARDEN
   Part 1: The Summons
═══════════════════════════════════════════════ */

The summons comes before dawn.

A single word scratched onto parchment in Aldric's brutal hand, delivered under my chamber door by a servant who has the good sense to knock once and flee. //Come.//

I groan and roll over, and then I feel it.

The sheets drag across my chest, and two points of sharp, bright sensitivity flare beneath the linen like sparks struck from flint. I freeze, one hand braced against the mattress, the other hovering over the left side of my chest where the sensation blooms hottest. The nipple is tender, not the flat, ignorable nub it has been all my life, but something raised, swollen, exquisitely aware of the fabric sliding across it.

I press my fingers there, gently. The flesh beneath yields, soft, warm, a small mound of new tissue that was not there a fortnight past. Not large. Not yet anything anyone would call a breast, but //present//, present enough that the roughness of linen feels like a tongue dragging over a fresh burn.

<<speech "mc">>Damn you, Thalara,<</speech>>

I mutter to the ceiling.

The ceiling offers no sympathy. Ceilings seldom do.

I swing my legs from the bed and stand, and the world tilts by a degree so subtle I might have imagined it, were it not for the faint pull of unfamiliar weight at my chest and the way my hips, wider this week than last, shift the axis of my balance as I rise. I steady myself against the bedpost. The wood is cold against a palm that is smoother than it should be, calluses thinning, the skin beneath them finer grained, as though someone is slowly sanding away the prince and revealing something underneath.

I cross to the wardrobe. My old training leathers hang inside, the chest piece, the bracers, the trousers, the boots. I have worn them a hundred times, a thousand. They smell of sweat and oil and the Iron Garden's particular blend of dust and blood. They smell like //me//.

Or they used to.

[[Dress for training|warrior_queen_day_1_2]]


:: warrior_queen_day_1_2

I pull the trousers on first. They fit, mostly. The waist is slightly loose where my midsection has narrowed, but the hips are snug, not painfully so, but the leather that once slid up without resistance now needs a shimmy, a tug, and a muttered curse as I work the material over hip bones migrating outward by the day. The seat is tighter too, the leather pulling across a backside that is, gods help me, //rounder// than it was.

I lace the waist and ignore the way the trousers hug curves that a prince's trousers were never designed to hug.

The chest piece comes next. This is where the morning's first true battle happens.

The leather breastplate is flat, designed for a male chest, for the broad, hard plane of pectoral muscle I have maintained through years of training. I lift it, press it against my torso, and begin lacing the sides.

The leather sits on the budding swells of my chest like a plank laid over two stones. The pressure is immediate and unpleasant, the stiff hide compressing tender, swollen tissue against my ribs, the new nipples grinding against leather that offers no give, no accommodation, no acknowledgment that there is something //there// now that needs space.

I lace tighter, wincing. If I can just flatten them, press the new flesh back into the chest wall, maybe they will behave. Maybe I can pretend, for one more morning, that the body beneath this armour is the body I have always known.

The left nipple sends a jolt of protest through my ribs and I gasp.

I stop lacing. Breathe through my teeth. Adjust the chest piece a fraction to the left, then the right, searching for a position that does not feel like wearing a punishment.

There is no such position. The breasts, //budding// breasts, I correct myself savagely, they are barely anything, refuse to be ignored.

<<speech "mc">>Fine,<</speech>>

I tell them, as though they are listening.

<<speech "mc">>But you shall behave yourself in the yard, or I swear by every god that ever drew breath, I shall bind you with rope and leather until you are flat as flagstone.<</speech>>

They offer no reply. But the left one throbs gently, as if in disagreement.

[[Head to the Iron Garden|warrior_queen_day_1_3]]


:: warrior_queen_day_1_3

The corridor outside my chamber is empty. The castle's servants know better than to linger near the heir's quarters before dawn. But as I pass the junction with the maid's corridor, a door opens and Maera's sharp, dark curled head emerges.

She takes one look at me, leathers, sword belt, hair hastily knotted, the expression of someone being dragged to their own execution, and leans against the doorframe with her arms folded.

<<speech "maera">>Training leathers. Before dawn. You look like a kicked dog someone has put into armour.<</speech>>

<<speech "mc">>Aldric summoned me.<</speech>>

<<speech "maera">>Mmhm, and you are wearing the old chest piece.<</speech>>

<<speech "mc">>It is the only chest piece I have.<</speech>>

She pushes off the doorframe and steps into the corridor. Her eyes, quick, dark, merciless in the way only a childhood friend's eyes can be, drop to my chest. Specifically, to the way the flat leather breastplate sits on what is beneath it. She does not stare. She //assesses//.

<<speech "maera">>It does not fit you anymore.<</speech>>

<<speech "mc">>It fits fine.<</speech>>

<<speech "maera">>Caelan. I can see the shape of your nipples pressing through the leather. If I can see them from here, every soldier in the yard will see them from there.<</speech>>

Heat rushes up my neck and into my face like a flame climbing a wick. I look down, and she is right. The new nipples, larger and more prominent than they were even a week ago, press outward against the flat leather, creating two small, unmistakable points that no amount of lacing can conceal.

<<speech "mc">>I... did not notice.<</speech>>

<<speech "maera">>Men never do. Not until someone else notices for them.<</speech>>

She says it without cruelty, with the wry, matter-of-fact tone of a woman stating an obvious truth.

<<speech "maera">>Here.<</speech>>

She disappears into her chamber and returns a moment later with a strip of thick, soft linen, the kind used for binding wounds. Without asking permission, she steps close and begins folding the linen into a wide band.

<<speech "maera">>Lift your arms.<</speech>>

<<speech "mc">>Maera, I do not need  <</speech>>

<<speech "maera">>Lift. Your. Arms.<</speech>>

I lift my arms. She reaches around me, passes the linen band across my chest, directly over the sensitive buds, and pulls it snug. The fabric compresses the new tissue against my ribs, not painfully, but firmly. The nipples, padded by the linen's thickness, no longer grind against the rough leather. The small mounds of flesh press flat, not invisible, but less obvious. Less //present//.

<<speech "maera">>There,<</speech>>

she says, tucking the end of the band. Her hands are quick and impersonal, a maid's hands performing a practical task.

<<speech "maera">>That will hold for the morning. When you are done being beaten by Aldric, come find me. We shall talk about getting you a proper binding.<</speech>>

<<speech "mc">>A binding?<</speech>>

<<speech "maera">>Yes. Like the ones washerwomen use when their breasts are sore from milk. Or like the ones soldiers' wives use when they ride long distances. Or  <</speech>>

